      en: "St. George's Church in Kaunas is a Roman Catholic church built in the Neo-Gothic style, consecrated in 1890. It was financed by the local German community. During WWII it suffered damage, and after the war it was closed by Soviet authorities and used as a warehouse. In 1988 it was reopened and restored. The church features a 60-meter tower, valuable stained glass windows, and a 19th-century organ. It stands as a testament to Kaunas's multicultural history and remains an active parish.",
