      en: "The Basilica in Krakinava is a Roman Catholic church in the town of Krakinava, Lithuania. It was built between 1901 and 1904 in Gothic Revival style and consecrated in 1905. Pope John Paul II elevated it to minor basilica in 2000. The interior features ornate altars and an organ. It is an important pilgrimage site, especially for the veneration of Our Lady of Krakinava. The crypt contains tombs of local bishops. The building is a protected architectural monument. The basilica plays a central role in the spiritual life of the region.",
