      en: "The White Synagogue in Joniškis is a significant Jewish heritage site in Lithuania. Built in the 18th century in Baroque style, it is painted white, hence its name. It served as the religious center for the Jewish community, which formed a large part of the population before WWII. After the Holocaust, it fell into disrepair. Restoration began in the 1990s. Today it functions as a museum and cultural center, housing an exhibition on Lithuanian Jewish history. It is one of the few surviving synagogues in the region.",
